IMPORT prelude

-- Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 (NT) -- the calendar arithmetic of this encoding, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library.
--
-- READINGS, none of them stated by the Act (the Interpretation Act 1978 (NT) is not deposited):
--   * "within 6 months after" a day (s 10(5), s 13(1)): the period ends on the same day of the month 6 months later, or
--     on that month's last day where it is shorter (31 August plus 6 months is 28 or 29 February). An act on that last
--     day is within the period; the next day is not.
--   * a person "attains the age of 18 years" (s 10(3)(e)(i)) on the 18th anniversary of the day of birth; a person born
--     on 29 February attains it on 28 February in a common year.
--
-- Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted from an unofficial copy under
-- the NT copyright policy of 8 October 1996 and the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Compensation (Fatal Injuries) Act 1974 (NT)`

-- A date from day, month and year, so that the case file can write dates without the daydate library.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS n)

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the first day` `to` `the second day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the second day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller number of` a `and` b MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- READING (above): the same day of the month n months later, or that month's last day where it is shorter.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus months` n MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (`the smaller number of` (DATE_DAY `the day`) `and` (`the number of days in month` `the new month` `of` `the new year`)) `the new month` `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the new year`    MEANS FLOOR (`the month count` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the new month`   MEANS (`the month count` MINUS (`the new year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

-- READING (above): the last day of a period of 6 months after a day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of 6 months after` `the day` MEANS `the day` `plus months` 6

-- READING (above): the day a person born on a day attains the age of 18 years.
GIVEN `the date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day of the 18th birthday of` `the date of birth` MEANS `the date of birth` `plus months` 216
